Subject: [PATCH 2/8] fix(trace): judge enlarged-grid paper counters as the
 walker traces them (ADR-392)

Outside this package's files: a minimal change to contour-support.ts from
main's #880, flagged for the integrator.

Operator change: none by itself. On an enlarged working grid,
restoreEnlargedContourSupport restores a paper counter from the native
mask when enlargement erased it. It grouped paper 4-connected, while the
outline walker joins two paper pixels across a corner wherever paper is
the scarcer colour there. A one-pixel notch of a counter that touches it
only at such a corner was therefore judged as a counter of its own and
patched back with the bilinear support field, even though the counter it
belongs to survived. Grouping now uses the walker's own test
(paperJoinsDiagonally), so a counter is judged whole.

Found through trace-supersample-support ("keeps Smooth bilinear
measurements outside erased detail"), which failed once crack filling
grouped slivers the walker's way; this commit keeps it passing. The new
contour-input test fails on main's contour-support.ts and passes here.

